 are unnecessary. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" already checks equality on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"set"},{"text":". Unconditional assignment is safe.","type":"text"}]}],"style":"note","type":"aside"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Dispatch-Loop-Detection","text":"Dispatch Loop Detection","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" warns if "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":" is called more than 100 times per debounce interval. This usually means "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"send()"},{"type":"text","text":" isn’t using the snapshot pattern, causing cascading re-renders that trigger re-dispatches."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Reducer-Weight","text":"Reducer Weight"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers run synchronously on the MainActor. Move O(n²) work into an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"text":" and dispatch the result back as an action.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Effect-Threading","text":"Effect Threading"},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effects run on Swift concurrency’s cooperative thread pool via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task { @concurrent in }"},{"type":"text","text":". Blocking calls ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Process.waitUntilExit()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DispatchSemaphore.wait()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Thread.sleep()"},{"type":"text","text":") hold threads hostage. If enough block, the pool starves and the MainActor freezes."}]}],"style":"important","name":"Important"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use async alternatives: "},{"code":"termi